---
code: transport-session-lost
when-fires: a session produced no completion marker, so whether the remote artifact ran is unknown. cli/transport_edge.rs, both phases. {host} is the destination, {attempts} how many were made, {diagnosis} a decision-inert reading of what severed it.
why: 26A stop-2 plus rul-integrity-failure-withholds-mutation. Absence of output cannot prove absence of execution, so this is neither clean nor failed. Sibling of transport-spawn-refused by WORLD STATE, not grammar: there nothing ran and the repair is the invocation, here something may have run and the repair is to re-probe.
---
-- webhost.sh --
#!/bin/sh
hork provision

-- edge-fault --
transport session-lost

-- replay --
$ dorc plan --host web1.example.net --book=webhost.sh
transport: error[transport-session-lost]: The session to web1.example.net ended
without its completion marker (the session ended without a status; attempts: 3),
so Dorc cannot tell whether the shipped artifact ran -- re-run `dorc plan` to
measure what actually happened.

$ dorc-loom --this vars
case: transport-session-lost
{{host}} = "web1.example.net"
{{diagnosis}} = "the session ended without a status"
{{attempts}} = "3"
